    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0180" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg106"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1186.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi>, </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-04-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 19, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith a copy of the London
                    Times of the 18th instant, containing a report of the proceedings in the suit
                    against the steamers Sumter and Rappahannock. I presume that a more full report
                    will be made by the professional gentlemen engaged on behalf of the government
                    through Mr. Dudley, the consul at Liverpool, who, in the absence of Mr. Cushing,
                    has had these matters in charge.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d85-a1.xml" xpointer="d85-a1"/>
            </div>
